{"id":56816,"ord":176,"n_segments":179,"prev":56815,"next":56817,"doc":{"id":"68154","title":"68154_Gus Johnson oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Gus Johnson","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/68154/","url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68154"},"chapter":"Drummers, favorites and closing","title":"Johnny Hodges, Cootie Williams and other favorites","category":"reflections","summary":"He calls Hodges his top alto man and praises Cootie, Freddy Webster and Snooky.","period":null,"year_from":null,"year_to":null,"words":179,"start":[341,4],"end":[342,15],"url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68154#s56816","tags":{"places":[],"venues":[],"bands":[{"name":"Jimmie Lunceford Orchestra","focus":0,"leader":"Jimmie Lunceford"}]},"people":[{"name":"Johnny Hodges","qid":"Q455176","n":4},{"name":"Snooky Young","qid":"Q2004076","n":3},{"name":"Freddy Webster","qid":"Q371982","n":3},{"name":"Charlie Parker","qid":"Q103767","n":2},{"name":"Cootie Williams","qid":"Q523899","n":1}],"story":{"theme":35,"theme_name":"Remembering the early trumpeters and their styles","community":77,"community_name":"Trumpeters I admired: rating the horn players","core":false},"blocks":[{"p":341,"b":4,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Johnny Hodges was my top alto man."},{"p":341,"b":5,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah, yes, he was."},{"p":341,"b":6,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Nobody had his sound."},{"p":341,"b":7,"s":"MS.","x":"But it's funny, Gus, so today when people talk about alto, they certainly are never going to forget Bird, but a lot of them forget Johnny."},{"p":341,"b":8,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Right, they do."},{"p":341,"b":9,"s":"MS.","x":"It's a sad thing, a very peculiar thing. Because nobody could touch him."},{"p":341,"b":10,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"And Bird loved Johnny."},{"p":341,"b":11,"s":"MS.","x":"Did he?"},{"p":341,"b":12,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Oh, yes, he did."},{"p":341,"b":13,"s":"MS.","x":"Oh, he did, did he?"},{"p":341,"b":14,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Yes, he did. Yes, sure."},{"p":341,"b":15,"s":"MS.","x":"That's very nice to know. Well, Johnny was unique. Simply nobody -- it was a God-given talent, wasn't it?"},{"p":342,"b":0,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Sure."},{"p":342,"b":1,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah."},{"p":342,"b":2,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"And Cootie Williams, there's something else."},{"p":342,"b":3,"s":"MS.","x":"Oh, yeah. Such a lead, he could command and that force and that play with that sound."},{"p":342,"b":4,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"And that command. First trumpet player, to me."},{"p":342,"b":5,"s":"MS.","x":"Marvelous, oh, yeah. He led that brass section over that whole band."},{"p":342,"b":6,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"That's right."},{"p":342,"b":7,"s":"MS.","x":"That was being driven."},{"p":342,"b":8,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"And Webster, that played trumpet with Lunceford --"},{"p":342,"b":9,"s":"MS.","x":"Freddy Webster."},{"p":342,"b":10,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Freddy Webster, yeah."},{"p":342,"b":11,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah."},{"p":342,"b":12,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"And then, Snookie."},{"p":342,"b":13,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah."},{"p":342,"b":14,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"[There's] Snookie sitting back there with the --"},{"p":342,"b":15,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah, Snookie's -- yeah, he could."}]}